Let f: X ⊆ R² -> R be a scalar-valued function of two variables. 
The section of the graph of f by the plane x = c (where c is a constant) is the set of points (x, y, z), where z = f(x, y) and x = c. 
Symbolized, 

	Section by x = c is {(x, y, z) ∈ R³ | z = f(x, y), x = c}. 

Similarly, the section of the graph of f by the plane y = c is the set of points described as follows: 

	Section by y = c is {(x, y, z) ∈ R³ | z = f(x, y), y = c}. 
